WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>A Clash of Masters</b>

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:49.060
Eva-chan, take this please.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:49.790
Yes, sir!

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:53.660
<b>Holger (50)
Blacksmith Guild Meister</b>

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.670
Taishou, could I see that knife for a moment?

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:57.430
Here you go.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.720
Amazing.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:05.460
This luster, this shine, this sharpness!

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.670
It doesn't even feel like 
it's from this world.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:18.560
<b>Eva (14)
Dishwasher at Nobu.
Resident of Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.690
You're Eva-chan, right?

00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:13.590
You also understand how wonderful 
this knife is, don't you?

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:14.610
I don't.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:18.240
Look at the cut made on this sashimi.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:23.560
<b>Maguro (Tuna) Sashimi</b>

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:23.560
<b>Cutting it with a good knife 
makes all the difference</b>

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:21.020
Isn't it so beautiful?

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:23.570
Not a hint of anything being crushed.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:26.820
The hallmark of a sharp blade.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.200
I've never seen a more magnificent knife.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.860
That's how excellent it is.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:40.600
Um, Taishou-san needs that 
knife to make more sashimi.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.380
My apologies, Taishou!

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:46.130
I'm a blacksmith, so this had 
me completely enthralled

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:47.750
on a craftsmanship level.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:53.470
Looking at this sashimi,
I can also tell that Taishou

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:56.510
is a masterful user of this wonderful tool.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.270
It melts in your mouth!

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:09.400
This food called sashimi 
is a true delicacy!

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.240
<b>Sharp</b>

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.600
And this alcohol called reishu 
that you recommended me...

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.730
This is also really great!

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:20.250
<b>Reishu</b>

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:20.250
<b>I could really go for a nicely 
chilled cup right now</b>

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.250
Thank you very much.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:24.100
I'm the representative for 
the Blacksmith Guild.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:28.630
<b>Nobu</b>

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:28.620
That's where a man named Gernot 
recommended this place to me.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.320
Gernot-san, you say?

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.110
That's right.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.900
He said he had eaten some different 
kind of pasta dish here.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:37.700
Pasta? Here?

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:42.370
Either way...

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:45.990
A restaurant with a master using the best 
tools to create the most delicious dishes,

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.790
and serving me wonderful sake.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:52.130
I've fallen in love with this place.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.680
Welcome!

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:58.820
Oh, you must be the famous Shinobu-chan.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:01.800
Hans told me about this place.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:06.800
<b>Nobu</b>

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.200
Could you be Hans-san's father?

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.800
I'm glad you came!

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.660
Please have a seat.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:10.670
<b>Lorenz (50)
Glass Craft Guild Meister</b>

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:17.070
Hey, if it isn't Lorenz, 
the clumsy glassblower.

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:23.060
And what's Holger the crybaby doing
drinking in a place like this?

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:27.210
I think it's none of your business 
where I choose to drink.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:31.580
Exactly my sentiment, my dear Holger-san!

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:32.650
What's that?!

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.930
For today's appetizer, we have edamame!

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.940
For today's appetizer, we have edamame!

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.670
My apologies, miss.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:57.840
Look at you. You made this poor 
little girl uncomfortable.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:01.960
You better carve this deep into 
that glass-filled head of yours.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:04.130
That little girl is called Eva-chan.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:21.790
Since you seem to like dry sake, 
please do try this as well.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:25.970
<b>Sharp</b>

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.410
Look at this, Lorenz!

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:31.760
I bet not even Hugo from your place, no,

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:34.580
I bet not even you could 
make a glass like this!

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:39.870
Well, if you're going to be like 
that, look at Taishou's knife.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:44.890
Neither you nor your father have 
ever made anything like it.

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:46.390
What's that?!

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.270
Thank you for waiting!

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:52.320
I've got salt-baked ayu and mackerel.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:50.900
<b>Salt-Baked Ayu</b>

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:50.900
<b>The crispy skin is very 
aromatic. It's an adult taste</b>

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:52.900
<b>Salt-Baked Mackerel</b>

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:52.900
<b>An izakaya mainstay.
 Do not skip the meat near the bone</b>

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:57.320
So good.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:01.360
The ayu I ordered is way better 
at satisfying an adult's palate

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:04.460
than the mackerel you ordered.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.050
<b>Rip rip rip rip</b>

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.050
Yeah right.

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:10.610
The fatty mackerel paired 
with whatsontap is clearly—

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.190
<b>Fizz</b>

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:18.510
The best!

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:21.180
Ayu with reishu is also the best.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:22.220
What was that?!

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:23.470
You talking to me?!

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:24.640
Uh, excuse me!

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.400
Then let me try a bite.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.270
Sure, try it.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:29.900
I'm going to try your mackerel.

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:37.970
This salt-baked ayu is really good.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:40.430
So is the mackerel you ordered.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:47.000
This special aroma and this slight 
bitter taste... is it the guts?

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.720
That's real good, too!

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:54.220
I like the contrast between the juicy flesh

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:56.460
and the crispiness around the bones.

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:58.340
<b>Fizz</b>

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:01.450
What do you think?

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:02.820
Pretty good, huh?

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:06.690
You also seem to be enjoying 
that salt-baked ayu.

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:11.350
Then let's see who can order the 
best fit for the whatsontap.

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:12.470
You're on.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:13.480
Shinobu-san!

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:14.290
Yes!

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:15.870
I'll have the croquettes!

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:18.180
And I'll have the thick-cut bacon!

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:19.930
Coming right up.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:23.710
Here's the cheese croquettes 
and the thick-cut bacon.

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:24.700
<b>Thick-cut Bacon</b>

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:24.700
<b>Also serves as Taishou's late night snack.
 Try it grilled, with mustard!</b>

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:24.700
<b>Cheese Croquettes</b>

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:24.700
<b>Cut it and watch the cheese ooze out.
 Enjoy these tasty croquettes.</b>

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:25.460
And two draft beers.

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:31.470
<b>Sizzle sizzle</b>

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:31.470
<b>Melt</b>

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.970
<b>Fizz</b>

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.970
<b>Fizz</b>

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.610
So good!

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:39.500
No, the bacon I ordered is better!

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:44.010
You're saying it can beat my 
croquettes-whatsontap combination?

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:45.770
Then lemme try that.

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:46.890
And I'm trying yours.

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:51.590
Eva-chan, what do we do
if those two start fighting?

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:53.020
I wouldn't worry about it.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:57.030
They're just having fun.

00:06:57.530 --> 00:07:00.030
My siblings are exactly the same.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:02.980
Hey! She ate the big piece of cheese!

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:05.920
Spit it out!

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:06.010
Hey, now!

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:11.210
Hey, he took my soup!

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.400
Stop it right now!

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:23.700
I knew it. My cheese croquettes are better.

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:27.610
Weren't you just talking about how 
the juicy bacon is irresistible?

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:32.820
Nobody fights for real when 
they're eating delicious food.

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:35.780
You know, though...

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:38.480
If I tried hard enough, I think 
I could make a glass like this.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:43.610
But you know, the glasses here 
are all exactly the same size.

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:48.530
Making multiple of these at this high 
quality is another story entirely.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:55.030
Noticing that is the first step
to being an artisan, though.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:59.730
Before you came, I was 
looking at Taishou's knife.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:03.740
I was honestly surprised by 
the quality of the craftsmanship.

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:06.600
It's not like you to admit weakness.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.830
I'm sure you could manage 
to make one at some point.

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:12.330
I'm sure you could, too.

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:17.110
<b>Sizzle</b>

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:17.110
<b>Sizzle</b>

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:17.110
What's this intense smell?

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:19.880
<b>Sizzle</b>

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:19.880
<b>Sizzle</b>

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:31.610
Here you go.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:35.730
<b>Nobu's Special Leftover Omu Soba</b>

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:35.730
<b>Soba noodles fried in sauce and gently
 covered in egg — it'll fill you right up!</b>

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:35.730
This is Nobu's special leftover omu soba.

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:38.540
Wow, it looks so good!

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:47.250
Thank you for making this 
for me, but I'm not hungry.

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:49.170
What's that?

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.630
Well if you don't want it, I'll eat it!

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:54.810
No, I was just thinking about 
ordering one last thing.

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:56.560
I'll have that.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:57.230
What?

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:57.960
Huh?!

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:04.700
I bet you want to give this to 
your little brother and sister.

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:10.120
Your siblings are going through 
 growth spurts, aren't they?

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:18.810
Don't worry. I'm sure Taishou will 
make you something nice to take home.

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:19.500
Right?

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:22.950
Something that's good even 
when it's gotten cold.

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:25.290
So don't worry and eat up!

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.580
Y-Yes, sir!

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:28.340
Thank you so much!

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:41.130
<b>Creamy</b>

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:41.120
Creamy, rich egg wrapped around 
soft yakisoba noodles!

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:43.290
That looks good.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:47.490
Uh... as adults, I don't think we can beg now.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:50.760
Don't worry. I'm sure Taishou 
will make you some, too,

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:53.290
if you're good boys.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:56.900
Yeah! All right!

00:09:56.900 --> 00:10:00.280
I came to the store first though.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:02.570
I'd like to order my portion first.

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:03.660
Hold on!

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.910
I was the first one to say I wanted some!

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.330
Obviously, I'm getting mine first!

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:11.420
Why don't you just eat your cold bacon?

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:12.510
What's that?

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:13.650
What?!

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:17.930
Both of you! Mind your manners 
while you're eating!

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:19.380
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:20.920
R-Right...

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:27.320
That's a big sister for you.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.280
Next up is Nobu Plus!

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:40.030
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:38.390
Those dishes you love to eat at 
restaurants, once you know the trick,

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:41.250
you can easily make them at home, too!

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:47.050
Ryuuta Kijima is going to put his own 
spin on the dishes featured in Nobu!

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:47.040
<b>Ryuuta Kijima Creates Nobu Dishes</b>

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:51.710
Eva-chan had an unexpected reveal 
as an older sister.

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:52.360
<b>Eva</b>

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:52.660
She is pretty strict.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:11:00.050
<b>Ryuuta Kijima</b>

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:55.890
She was the little kid, but 
at home, that's how she is.

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:56.210
<b>Grew up in a household where both his grandmother and his mother were culinary researchers,
so he got into cooking at an early age. Now he's a culinary researcher who's popular
for his simple but serious recipes and his fun presentation.</b>

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:58.370
The omu soba? That 
looked super good, so...

00:10:58.370 --> 00:10:58.850
I know!

00:10:58.850 --> 00:11:04.220
I deliberately won't put my spin on it and 
just make it how I think would be good.

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:04.390
<b>Ryuuta Kijima Style
Standard Omu Soba</b>

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:09.410
Making a good omu soba at home is actually 
pretty hard. What's the secret?

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:09.410
<b>Standard Omu Soba
 [Ingredients (serves 1)]
 Fried soba noodles   1 portion
 Sausages   2
 Cabbage   50 grams
 Egg   2

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:12.060
I'll use two cabbage leaves today.

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:22.740
<b>Standard Omu Soba</b>

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:12.800
All right.

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:18.590
Cut the sausage so the surface 
area is big, like this.

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:20.540
The thing that always strikes me about Nobu

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:22.310
is that their "staff meals" 
are always super good.

00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:22.760
Totally!

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:24.640
Our staff meals are definitely more basic.

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:25.110
Oh, yeah?

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:30.470
So about these noodles, warm them in the 
microwave for about a minute first.

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:34.940
<b>Cut the pouch and warm the noodles 
for 1 minute in the microwave</b>

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:30.830
Okay.

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:34.670
The reason is that the noodles will stay 
clumped together if they are cold.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:38.200
Oh, I see. That's an important point!

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:39.320
First, the sausage.

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.390
Then the cabbage.

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:44.560
It's already starting to smell good!

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:50.020
The sausage release a lot of 
umami if you fry the cut edges.

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:52.220
<b>Fry the cut edges of the 
sausages to release the umami</b>

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:52.060
That then goes onto the other ingredients.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:52.540
I like it.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:56.390
They're getting browned now. 
You can add the noodles at this point.

00:11:56.390 --> 00:11:56.890
Roger.

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:59.910
Since we warmed them before, 
they come apart nicely.

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:00.850
I see!

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:03.810
Fold the other ingredients in 
as you stir-fry the noodles.

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:06.840
And we add the sauce powder packet.

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:09.520
Oh wow, we're already almost done!

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:13.080
Once the noodles are all nice 
and unclumped, it's done.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.100
So we put it aside for now.

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:17.050
Then, make the frying pan really hot.

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:17.750
How hot?

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:21.840
Look out for the oil running 
quickly like this.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.840
You can put a bit of egg on 
the tip of the chopsticks and

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:26.590
<b>Heat the frying pan so that egg from 
the chopsticks solidifies right away</b>

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:28.660
drag them across the pan like this. 
It should solidify right away.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:26.580
That's pretty hot!

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:32.800
Then we put all of the egg in. Dump 
it in and mix it in a big motion.

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:38.470
<b>After putting the egg in, mix and make the 
center thicker, then turn off the burner</b>

00:12:33.490 --> 00:12:38.170
Try to get a bit more in the 
center. Then turn off the burner.

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:38.730
Really?

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:42.530
Then we put the fried noodles on the center.

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:46.530
We drape the egg from 
here to the other side.

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:50.080
Then we push it all to the edge of the pan.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:54.430
<b>After putting the yakisoba in the middle,
slide all of the egg toward the edge of the frying pan</b>

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.110
You just have to push it over?

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:54.440
If the egg isn't still a bit raw, 
it won't stick to the noodles.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:58.140
Once you have your plate ready, 
just flip the pan over.

00:12:58.140 --> 00:12:58.650
Done!

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:02.800
Use a paper towel to 
press it into the right shape.

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:06.810
<b>As a finishing touch, use 
a paper towel to fix the shape</b>

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:05.170
Done!

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:06.660
So easy, so pretty!

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:08.590
Add ketchup and mayonnaise.

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:10.350
It's not complete without that.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:16.180
Here are the tips: microwave the noodles 
beforehand so they don't clump together.

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:19.980
<b>Standard Omu Soba</b>

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:20.880
And the egg will quickly set if you don't 
finish it up in one go, so be swift.

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:22.390
Please give this a go.

00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:24.110
I recommend eating it hot, 
right when it's done.

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:26.980
Fluffy egg and the fried 
noodles are a perfect match!

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.860
If you get the tricks 
down, anyone can do it!

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:32.300
It pairs perfectly with beer, too!

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:58.010
<b>Next Time...   
Beauty and the Abura-age</b>

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:54.330
Next time on "Isekai Izakaya"
aka "Izakaya Nobu in Aitheria."

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:53.810
<b>Crunch</b>

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:57.550
Please sample the tasty tales.
